==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|curuner|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|custos placitorum coronae||guardian of the crown's pleas|lang=la}}. The function was originally to protect royal properties.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈkɒ.ɹə.nə(r)/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒrənə(r)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[public]] [[official]] who presides over an [[inquest]] into [[unnatural]] [[death]]s.
# {{context|Canada|US|lang=en}} A [[medical doctor]] who performs [[autopsies]] and determines time and cause of [[death]] from a scientific standpoint.
# The [[administrative]] [[head]] of a [[sheading]].

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|who presides over an inquest}} [[medical examiner]], [[ME]] {{qualifier|if he performs autopsies}}

